From f823b1883e4dd3d36fa9de841345bdc01101632f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rehanraza786 <rehanraza786@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:26:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/12] Assertions cannot forge provenance either; find_callers
 says when it is guessing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the class rather than the instance. docs/graph-assertions.json is
committed and therefore attacker-controlled in any repo that takes PRs, and
the ingest copied its author field verbatim into both assertions.author and
the msg_edges/db_access source column — so an entry could write
author:"parser" and read as a parsed fact, the same hole just fixed for
insights. Author is now clamped to a display-safe token, reserved words
(parser, ariadne, scip, tree-sitter, indexer) are prefixed 'claimed-',
confidence is constrained to high|medium|low instead of stored as given,
and evidence is length-capped.

find_callers already told agents it was heuristic — in its description, and
in the message it returns when it finds nothing. Neither helps an agent
holding a plausible-looking list of callers. It now carries the warning on
populated results, and only when SCIP actually has compiler-resolved data
for that symbol, so the hint costs nothing when it could not be acted on.

run_tests.py: a committed assertion cannot forge parser provenance.
